BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Black holes: tides</h1>
A delta-glider falls from rest, 20,000 km out, towards a black hole of 10 solar masses
(spin 0.7), with the damage model on: thousands of kilometres out the
tides tear its parts off, then the rest, long before the horizon (25
km). The pieces fall on in the hole's spacetime.
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System BlackHoleSmallTest
  Date MJD 51982.6685767396
  Script Tests/BlackHoleTidesTest
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship TIDE
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET TIDE
  MODE Extern
  POS 4 0 -20
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 50.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_SHIPS
TIDE:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting SmallHole
  ELEMENTS 1.0e9 0.00000 0.0 0.0 0.0 0.0 51982.6685767396
  AROT 0 0 0
END
END_SHIPS
